  "question": {
    "text": "The equation of the curve lying in the first quadrant, such that the portion of the&nbsp;<math><mi>x</mi></math>-axis cut-off between the origin and the tangent at any point <math><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to the ordinate of <math><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo></math> is (where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math> is an arbitrary constant)"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Equation of the tangent at <math><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />is <math><mi>Y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Putting&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">'</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;is a linear differential equation.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ι</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>y</mi></mfrac></math><br />Thus, the solution is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">∫</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></math><br />or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>c</mi></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></math><br />Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mfrac></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></math>&nbsp;is the equation of the curve</p>"
  }
